t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tFact Sheets\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link is-current\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Releases\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tReleases\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/remarks/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Remarks\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tRemarks\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/research/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Research\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tResearch\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</ul>\n\t\t</div>\n\t</nav>\n\t</div>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center wp-block-paragraph\"><em>New Analysis <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/The-State-of-American-Manufacturing_Oct2026.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Confirms</a> President Trump’s Pro-Growth Policies Are Driving American Manufacturing Resurgence</em></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">President Donald J. Trump’s America First agenda is revitalizing American manufacturing, delivering historic investments, driving up wages, and igniting a blue-collar BOOM.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">After the Biden Administration lost more than 200,000 American manufacturing jobs in its final two years due to reckless Democrat polices, President Trump is delivering on his promise to put American workers first.&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"750\" height=\"444\" src=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/image.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-53242\" srcset=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/image.png 750w, https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/image.png?resize=600,355 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 750px) 100vw, 750px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The results speak for themselves. New analysis by the Council of Economic Advisors (CEA) reports that wages are rising faster than inflation, domestic manufacturing is expanding, and the blue-collar jobs lost under the Biden Administration are rightly returning back to U.S. soil. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"750\" height=\"429\" src=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/image_7340ae.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-53244\" srcset=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/image_7340ae.png 750w, https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/image_7340ae.png?resize=600,343 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 750px) 100vw, 750px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Wages are outpacing inflation under President Trump, reversing the $3,000 annual decline in real wages under Biden. Since President Trump took office, blue-collar workers are seeing even bigger gains: manufacturing wages are up <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/The-State-of-American-Manufacturing_Oct2026.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">$2,000 and construction wages $2,800</a>.&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Demand for factory construction workers is surging, hiring rising, and layoffs down over the past year. Overtime pay is also up— thanks to President Trump’s no-tax-on-overtime policy, workers are now keeping more of what they earn.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"750\" height=\"466\" src=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/image_4baa15.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-53246\" srcset=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/image_4baa15.png 750w, https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/image_4baa15.png?resize=600,373 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 750px) 100vw, 750px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The benefits of President Trump’s pro-growth agenda and successful tariff policies extend beyond factory floors. This resurgence is strengthening America’s position in critical industries essential to our national security, including aerospace, aircraft equipment, metals, and natural gas and petroleum production.&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A stronger manufacturing sector means more opportunities for American workers, higher wages, and business expansion that supports Main Street economies who support communities across the country.&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 id=\"h-investing-in-south-carolina-communities\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>BY THE NUMBERS</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>AMERICAN MANUFACTURING JOBS SURGING:</strong> Manufacturing <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/The-State-of-American-Manufacturing_Oct2026.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">employment is up</a> 72,000 in 2026, including a 101,000 job increase in durable goods, reversing losses of more than 200,000 manufacturing jobs during the Biden Administration’s last two years. Since President Trump took office, <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/The-State-of-American-Manufacturing_Oct2026.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">construction employment</a> has grown by 100,000, including <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/The-State-of-American-Manufacturing_Oct2026.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">more than</a> 111,000 additional factory construction jobs.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>RISE IN ANNUAL WAGES:</strong> Inflation-adjusted wages for blue-collar manufacturing workers have risen an average of $2,400 more per year since President Trump took office. Construction workers’ real wages are up <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/The-State-of-American-Manufacturing_Oct2026.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"> $3,800</a>.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>HIGHEST BUSINESS GROWTH IN 5 YEARS:</strong> U.S. business growth has reached its highest level in more than five years, while manufacturing expands and American goods exports are on track for a record year.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>NO TAX ON OVERTIME:</strong> American construction workers are keeping more of what they earn thanks to No tax on overtime, with more than 29 million Americans claiming the deduction this filing season.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>TRILLIONS IN INVESTMENTS SECURED:</strong> President Trump <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/The-State-of-American-Manufacturing_Oct2026.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">has secured</a> trillions of dollars in investment commitments across the United States, supporting domestic production, factory expansion, and American jobs.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>SMALL BUSINESS GROWTH:</strong> Small businesses and local economies <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/The-State-of-American-Manufacturing_Oct2026.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">are feeling</a> the benefits of President Trump’s manufacturing boom.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"></ul>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\" />\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><br><strong>President Trump is driving a new era of economic opportunity, industrial strength, and national prosperity—unleashing America’s Golden Age. </strong></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"></p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/2026/10/new-analysis-president-trumps-pro-growth-policies-ignite-manufacturing-resurgence/\">New Analysis: President Trump’s Pro-Growth Policies Ignite Manufacturing Resurgence</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov\">The White House</a>.</p>",
